From f9cd144a9e0bdc5595edaf516a8c0a678b23dbcb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: shota <monyuonyu@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 08:52:26 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 417/417] Translations (ja): enumerations shown translated, the
 rest of the strings

FEM: the words of enumerations in panels (boundary kinds, section types,
rigid body modes, result representations...) are shown through FemEnum;
what is written to the object is still the enumeration's word, by index or
item data. CAM: property labels, spindle/units/material combos, tool
types; summaries translate their template, not the filled-in string, and
say ? for an unset number of flutes instead of None. FEM examples dialog.

Strings no .ts carried (the site's copy is older) are in extra_ja.ts, read
only by make_fallback.py; labels wrongly marked notr in .ui files lose the
mark. Words of one field stay out of the fallback (Load is a force in FEM).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
